{
  "$Comment": "Hallow's Eve in the Almanac: the season's name and picture, its yearly keepsake, and the tallies it keeps. The file name is the calendar event id. Each stat line counts one kind of moment; LiveOnly false keeps the every-season tally running all year, for the bombs and geodes a player still holds after the event. Hero.Composition is the banner at the top of the season's page: each item's own icon drawn at X and Y (pixels from the top-left of the 962 x 240 plate) and Size (a square side up to 128; 64, 96 and 128 read best), over the Background colour. Keep the plate left of about x 450 clear for the title, status and dates. Gradient paints the sky from its Top colour down to its Bottom one in place of the flat Background, and Glow lays a soft round light under the items, its square box placed by X, Y and Size the way an item's is. Sections lays out the page below its top in the order written: the tallies, the items grid, the keepsake shelf, the achievements and the links. The grid (Collection.Items, at most 45, nine a row) shows every item a player can find this season; a Hidden one shows '?' until the player has held it once, and SourceKey is the tooltip line saying where it comes from. Add, drop or reorder a slot here; an item the server does not have is left out.",
